Classification: SINGLE_REVERSION_FRAGILE
Valid: true. Duplicate SHA256 1720274b10e7ecc5ef5a85965231a5c8335436ffd2e81f156791e89947bcb352.
Starting from the fully rescuing partner6 lesion on replicate8, every unique one-for-one reverse substitution toward replicate8 was tested at levels8..16.
Twelve reverse pairs failed at every level:
58->6, 50->6, 42->6, 26->6, 10->6,
2->6, 2->14, 2->22, 2->30, 2->38, 2->54, 2->62.
Many matched alternatives were universally rescuing; for example 10->14, 42->14, 42->22, 42->30, 42->54 and 42->62.
The explicit reverse edge 42->38 remained rescuing at levels8..11 but failed at levels12..16.
Interpretation: the fully rescued context has a structured but fragile local basin. Two standout factors are addition of replicate8 cell6 and removal of partner6 cell2; either appears in broad families of universal failures.
Plain speak: the repaired state is not generally brittle, but two particular cell changes are dangerous. Adding cell6 from the failing pattern or removing cell2 from the rescuing pattern repeatedly destroys recovery.
Next: decompose those two factors with one-sided add/remove arms and matched neutral controls so generic lesion-cardinality pressure is separated from cell-specific causality.
